@id n1_ranulf
# DRAFT
# Ranulf, the sacrist, at the candle stand in the nave at dusk (night 1). Dry, exact, never stops working.
# He keeps the bells, the candles, the relic and the incense. He offers nothing yet (the remedy is night 3).
# Hidden: he wears the horned costume; the relic is a pig's bone; the incense doses the choir.
== start
(The sacrist at the candle stand in the nave, trimming wicks with small shears. He doesn't stop.)
Ranulf {grave}: The porter. Ranulf, sacrist. The bell is mine. The ringing of it is yours. Don't be late with it.
-> topics

== again
Ranulf {grave}: Something else?
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n1_ranulf_candles] What should I know about the candles? -> candles
* [if not n1_ranulf_relic] Tell me about the relic. -> relic
* [if not n1_ranulf_incense] What's the incense for? -> incense

== candles [set n1_ranulf_candles]
Ranulf {grave}: Wax on the altar, tallow everywhere else. Every one is counted.
Ranulf {grave}: If you find a lamp out on your round, light it from the sanctuary lamp and tell me. Not the prior. Me.
-> topics

== relic [set n1_ranulf_relic]
Ranulf {grave}: The saint's finger, in the silver hand on the altar. Pilgrims may kiss the glass.
Ranulf {grave, glance}: I keep the key to it. Nobody opens it. Nobody needs to.
-> topics

== incense [set n1_ranulf_incense]
Ranulf {calm, glance}: At Matins I cense the choir. Breathe it in. It's the prayers going up.
Ranulf {grave}: And it's good for the chest, in this damp.
-> topics

== leave
Ranulf {grave}: The black ring, porter. Not after it.
